  "evicted": {
   "text": "<<on tending a rooftop beehive this season>>  \n\nthe season has brought a new sense of purpose to my work as a beekeeper. each morning, I rise before the sun to check on the hive, to listen for the gentle hum of the bees and to feel the warmth of the beeswax that they produce. the work is not just about survival, but about connection—between the bees and the land, between the bees and the people who care for them.  \n\nas the days grow longer and the weather becomes more favorable, the bees begin to thrive. their activity is a sign of life, a reminder that even in the quietest of moments, there is always something to be learned. i find myself reflecting on the importance of patience, of giving the bees the space they need to flourish.  \n\nthere is a beauty in the simplicity of this work. it is not about the grandeur of the hive, but about the quiet strength of the bees, their ability to work together in harmony. every time i see them buzzing around the flowers, i am reminded of the delicate balance that sustains life.  \n\nthis season has taught me that tending a beehive is more than a job—it is a practice of mindfulness, of respect, and of gratitude. it is a way of honoring the natural world and the creatures that share it. and as the season draws to a close, i leave with a deep sense of fulfillment, knowing that my work has made a difference.",
